mode: "100644"
text: "# The WATCH framework — scripts engineered for watch-through\n\nShort-form lives or dies on **watch-through**, so the script's only job is to be un-skippable. Each letter is a\ngate; most scripts fail at W (slow intro) or C (the payoff doesn't keep the promise).\n\n## W — Win the first 3 seconds\n~50–60% of drop-off is here, so this is the whole ballgame.\n- **Lead with the most striking frame** (text overlay / dramatic visual / mid-action) — something interesting is\n  on screen *before* the first word. No logo, no \"hey guys,\" no slow zoom on a static image.\n- **Layer the hook:** visual + on-screen text + verbal at once (~3× the hold of a single-element hook). One short,\n  specific, bold/curious sentence — outcomes/numbers/contrasts, not a vague topic.\n- **Shot-list 5 hook variants** over the same body; the hook is a variable to *test*, not a one-time decision.\n\n## A — Arc with open loops\nStructure = **Hook → Body/escalation → Payoff → CTA/loop.** Keep them watching:\n- A bridge sentence carries curiosity from hook into body; open a loop early (\"I'll come back to why this\n  matters\"); number the points so progress is visible (\"step 2 of 3\").\n- **Visual change every ~2–4s**; never hold a shot past ~3 sentences / ~8s without a change (pattern interrupts:\n  cut, zoom, B-roll, SFX).\n- **Cut anything that isn't earning the next second** — if a line doesn't grab, teach, or advance, delete it.\n\n## T — Two tracks (sound-off + sound-on)\n~80% watch on mute, so **write the muted version first.**\n- On-screen text/captions carry the story alone; VO/audio *adds* when sound is on. The three tracks (visual,\n  spoken, text) reinforce, never compete.\n- Captions from word one, legible (bold, high-contrast, 4–7-word chunks, safe zones). **Test the cut on mute** —\n  if the hook doesn't land silently, rewrite it.\n\n## C — Cash the promise\nThe payoff is *why they stayed* — the answer/reveal/punchline/transformation that **delivers what the hook sold.**\nIf the hook said \"3 changes that fixed my reach,\" the third (best) change must land. Over-promising tanks AVD and\ngets suppressed; a true promise kept is the cleanest path to reach.\n\n## H — Hold the loop, land the CTA\n- **Engineer the loop:** make the final frame/line flow back to frame 1 (a circular last subtitle: \"…and that's\n  why the first line mattered\") so replays feel intentional — replays compound distribution.\n- **One fitting CTA**, ≈2s, tied to value: save (\"you'll need this for step X\"), share, or follow for the next\n  part — never a rote \"like & subscribe\" that drags completion.\n- Then route platform specifics to `reels-script` / `tiktok-script` / `youtube-shorts`; **WoopSocial publishes**\n  the finished file.\n"
